### Direction J — @orqafy/jobs build pipeline (T2 ~15K, blocks worker in staging/prod)
   - Surfaced 2026-05-29 by staging compose dry-run (PR fix/web-transpile-workspace-packages, commit 997d1a5). Web fix shipped via that branch; worker still crash-loops at runtime.
   - Root cause: `packages/jobs/package.json` `exports` points at `./src/*.ts` instead of built `./dist/*.js`. Node 22 type-stripper rejects `.ts` files under `node_modules/` in the worker runner stage.
   - Scope: add `tsconfig.build.json` + `build` script to `packages/jobs`; rewrite `exports` to `./dist/*.js` paths; add `RUN pnpm --filter @orqafy/jobs build` to `apps/worker/Dockerfile` (and possibly `apps/web/Dockerfile`) before downstream builds; verify `pnpm --filter @orqafy/jobs build && pnpm --filter @orqafy/web test && pnpm --filter @orqafy/worker test` all clean; rebuild worker image and confirm boot via local dry-run.
   - Note: BullMQ is already non-functional on current main, so this is not a regression — but it is a hard blocker on the first real Komodo deploy if the worker is expected to process queues.
   - Suggested branch: `feat/jobs-build-pipeline`. May also need to revisit `apps/web/next.config.ts` transpilePackages once jobs ships built `.js` (the extensionAlias workaround may become unnecessary).
   - Full handoff in `.cline/handoffs/2026-05-29-staging-dryrun-session.md` (committed alongside the web fix).

