## Standing 9-point pre-flight (run before any code on any batch — REINFORCED)

1. `git status` + `git log -1` — confirm tree state.
2. `pnpm --filter @orqafy/web test` — confirm 747/747 GREEN baseline.
3. Read input Zod schema of any router procedure the batch claims to reuse.
4. If router newly READS a field, verify all existing tests on that path mock the field.
5. Grep schema.prisma for any model in scope; **emit four-quadrant verdict per model** (public+tid / public-only / no-schema+tid / no-schema-only). Never trust .whatsnext premise alone.
6. Confirm package.json has any third-party library called out in scope.
7. Re-read .claude/rules/memory-governance.md §1 for the tier classification.
8. Emit explicit branch-creation line item in the BUILD BATCH PROPOSAL.
9. For publicProcedure vs protectedProcedure claims, grep the router to verify. **Verify the EXACT test path against the router composition block (`createTRPCRouter({ key: subRouter })`) — model name often differs from mount key (e.g. `poRouter` mounts as `po:`).**


## Recurring-pattern lessons banked (apply at next batch PRE-FLIGHT)

- 🟢 publicProcedure tenant resolution — input.tenantSlug → db.tenant.findUnique
- 🟢 System-actor lookup for guest writes — webmaster via findFirst+orderBy createdAt asc
- 🟢 Rate-limit tier — rateLimiters.public.check(ip) at 10/min/IP for guest mutations
- 🟢 Auth-gated-lookup enumeration resistance — same NOT_FOUND for "wrong auth" vs "missing resource"
- 🟢 sanitizePlainText on user-facing text fields before storage
- ⚖️ Order-creation duplication tolerated — extraction deferred until 3rd variant
- 🔴 useCart() shape gotcha — destructure mismatch caught at typecheck
- 🟢 Intentional scope-trim — 8× consecutive single-direction batches
- 🟢 Helper-extract refactor pattern — protected→public dual-caller surfaces extract to src/lib/
- 🟢 RED-phase Zod-enum tightening — assert specific mock-side error marker + mock was-called
- 🟢 Atomicity through in-transaction external calls — external HTTP inside DB tx acceptable for payment surfaces
- 🟢 As-any cast cleanup post-GREEN — grep `as any` after implementation
- 🟢 BUILT-IN NODE:CRYPTO SUFFICES — node:crypto + aes-256-gcm is FIPS-approved AEAD
- 🟢 AES-256-GCM FORMAT — {iv}.{authTag}.{ciphertext} dot-separated base64url
- 🟢 LAZY ENV READ FOR TESTABILITY — getKey() reads process.env at CALL time
- 🟢 FILE-LEVEL RED — test file import of not-yet-created module fails entire file at load
- 🟢 (Batch 23): writeAuditLog inside $transaction — single atomic unit for order + stock movement + audit
- 🟢 (Batch 23): Server Component chip-row filter pattern — Link-based filters with hrefFor URL serialization
- 🟢 (Batch 23): Hoisted vi.mock pattern for new module export
- 🟢 NEW (Batch 24): Sibling-model tenantId backfill — UPDATE FROM parent table (ecommerce_order_items.tenant_id from ecommerce_orders.tenant_id via order_id JOIN) is cleaner than re-sourcing from tenants table. Works when parent already has NOT NULL tenant_id from a prior migration.
- 🟢 NEW (Batch 25): admin router ctx has no session.user — admin log lines omit actor; revisit when admin audit-log work surfaces
